"About attribution for GMV Max | TikTok Seller Center (https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-attribution-for-gmv-max?lang=en)\nciteturn554view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-attribution-for-gmv-max?lang=en\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 48\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Business Help Centre】 【2†Partner enablement】 【3†What's new】\nL3: \nL4: # About attribution for GMV Max\nL5: \nL6: Last updated: June 2026\nL7: \nL8: GMV Max is an automated ad campaign type that optimizes both paid and organic traffic for your TikTok Shop. When you create a GMV Max campaign, all relevant conversions will be attributed to GMV Max while the campaign is running.\nL9: ## About attribution for Product GMV Max\nL10: \nL11: When you create a Product GMV Max campaign, all paid and organic orders for the products you chose for your campaign will be attributed to GMV Max while the campaign is running. If someone orders a product featured in your GMV Max campaign while your campaign is running, the order will be attributed to GMV Max whether or not they engaged with one of your ads.\nL12: \nL13: Learn 【4†how to view reporting for your Product GMV Max campaign】.\nL14: ## About attribution for LIVE GMV Max\nL15: \nL16: When you create a LIVE GMV Max campaign, all paid and organic conversions in the LIVE event you chose for your campaign will be attributed to GMV Max. Orders from all shops during the LIVE event will be attributed to your LIVE GMV Max campaign, including orders from shops that weren't used to set up the GMV Max campaign. If someone leaves the LIVE event to place an order, this order will not be attributed to the LIVE GMV Max campaign.\nL17: ## Examples\nL18: \nL19: For example, say you're running a GMV Max campaign for Product A.\nL20: \nL21:   * If a customer views or clicks on an ad for Product A and then buys Product A within 1 day, the purchase will be attributed to GMV Max as long as the campaign is still active.\nL22: \nL23:   * If a customer views or clicks on an ad for Product A and then buys Product A 3 days later, the purhcase won't be attributed to GMV Max.\nL24:   * If a customer views or clicks on an ad for Product A and then buys Product A 3 days later, the purchase won't be attributed to GMV Max.\nL25: \nL26:   * If a customer views or clicks on an ad for Product A and then buys a different product from your shop, the purchase won't be attributed to GMV Max.\nL27: \nL28:   * If a customer purchases Product A while the GMV Max campaign is active, but doesn't view or click on any ads, the purchase will be attributed to GMV Max.\nL29: \nL30: 【5†Image†sf16-website-login.neutral.ttwstatic.com】\nL31: Log in for a personalised experience\nL32: \nL33: 【6†Sign up】\nL34: \nL35: Resources\nL36: \nL37: * 【7†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL38: * 【8†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL39: * 【9†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL40: * 【10†TikTok for Business】\nL41: * 【11†Creative Center】\nL42: * 【12†Agentic Hub】\nL43: \nL44: * 【13†Terms and Policies】\nL45: * 【14†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL46: \nL47: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout Event Deduplication | TikTok Ads Manager (https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/event-deduplication?lang=en)\nciteturn554view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/event-deduplication?lang=en\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 43\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Business Help Centre】 【2†Partner enablement】 【3†What's new】\nL3: # About event deduplication\nL4: \nL5: Last updated: May 2025\nL6: Event deduplication is required if you use both the TikTok Pixel and Events API to share duplicate copies of events, which report the exact conversion on their website. If we recognize that events overlap and are duplicate copies of the exact conversion, we will keep and enrich (see below) the first event to ensure that duplicate event counts do not occur for measurement and reporting purposes. You can use deduplicated events to help measure, optimize, and target your ads on TikTok.\nL7: ## Features\nL8: \nL9: You must share Event ID (event_id) as a parameter through both Pixel and Events API to ensure deduplication takes place. If TikTok recognizes that events overlap and duplicates of each other, we will record the first event received for measurement and reporting.\nL10: ## Key concepts\nL11: \nL12: Deduplication is not required if you share different events separately between the Pixel and the Events API, without event overlap. For example, sharing AddToCart events through the Pixel, and Purchase events through the Events API.\nL13: \nL14: Deduplication is required if you share the same events through the Pixel and the Events API, with event overlap. For example, sharing Purchase events through both Pixel and the Events API.\nL15: ## Examples\nL16: \nL17: There are three overlapping scenarios that can occur with events:\nL18: \nL19:   * Overlapping between Pixel events: We deduplicate any events shared through Pixel, with the identical event and event_id parameters arriving within a 48-hour window from the first event.\nL20: \nL21:   * Overlap between Events API events: We deduplicate any events shared through the Events API, with the identical event and event_id parameters arriving within a 48-hour window from the first event.\nL22:   * Overlap between Pixel and Events API events: We merge or deduplicate events shared by the Pixel and Events API with the identical event and event_id parameters arriving after 5 minutes and within a 48-hour window from the first event (if applicable).\nL23: \nL24: Learn more 【4†about developer documentation for event deduplication†business-api.tiktok.com】.\nL25: \nL26: 【5†Image†sf16-website-login.neutral.ttwstatic.com】\nL27: \nL28: Log in for a personalised experience\nL29: \nL30: 【6†Sign up】\nL31: \nL32: Resources\nL33: * 【7†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL34: * 【8†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL35: * 【9†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL36: * 【10†TikTok for Business】\nL37: * 【11†Creative Center】\nL38: \nL39: * 【12†Terms and Policies】\nL40: * 【13†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL41: \nL42: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBusiness Resource Centre (https://ads.us.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-tiktok-shop-ads-attribution)\nciteturn554view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.us.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-tiktok-shop-ads-attribution\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 73\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Business Help Centre】 【1†Partner enablement】 【2†What's new】\nL3: # About attribution for TikTok Shop Ads\nL4: \nL5: Last updated: August 2025\nL6: \nL7: For TikTok Shop Ads, attribution is the measure of how many orders resulted from someone viewing or clicking an ad. We use your unique Shop ID to attribute orders to your shop across all ad formats and placements, as well as 【3†ads using affiliate creative videos†ads.tiktok.com】.\nL8: \nL9: For example, if you create a Video Shopping Ad that uses an affiliate video linking to your product, then the orders are attributed to:\nL10:   * Orders for other products from your shop\nL11: \nL12:   * Orders from other sources including livestreams, product cards and search\nL13: \nL14:   * Orders that come through your Non-affiliate links\nL15: \nL16: Shop Ads dynamically optimizes your ads across all available placements, including the TikTok video feed, Search, and Shopping Center. We won't attribute an order to multiple TikTok Shop Ads. However, it is best to refer to onsite events to evaluate performance.\nL17: ## Attribution windows for TikTok Shop Ads\nL18: \nL19: The attribution window for TikTok Shop Ads is the length of time between when a person clicked or viewed your ad and then placed an order. We'll attribute an order to the ad someone interacted with most recently, with Clicks taking precedence over Views.\nL20:   * Clicks: 7-day attribution window. If someone clicks on your ad and places an order within 7 days, we'll attribute the order to your ad. If someone clicked on multiple ads within the same 7 days, we'll attribute the order to the most recent ad they clicked.\nL21:   * Views: 1-day attribution window. If someone views an ad and places an order within 24 hours, we'll attribute the order to your ad. If someone viewed multiple ads within the same 24 hours, we'll attribute the order to the most recent ad they viewed.\nL22: \nL23: In cases where someone both views and clicks different ads, the purchase is attributed to the ad they interacted with last, with clicks taking precedence over views.\nL24: Note: Seller center reports sales that happen on the day, whereas TikTok Ads Manager reports sales that have happened within the 7-day attribution window.\nL25: ### Example\nL26: \nL27: You have three ads for your TikTok Shop: Ad A, Ad B and Ad C.\nL28: \nL29:   1. On Monday, a customer clicks on Ad A but doesn't buy anything right away.\nL30: \nL31:   2. On Tuesday, the customer clicks on Ad B and still doesn't place an order.\nL32: \nL33:   3. On Wednesday, the customer views ad C but doesn't click on it.\nL34: \nL35:   4. Later on Wednesday, the customer goes back to your shop and places an order.\nL36: \nL37: The order will be attributed to Ad B, even though the customer viewed Ad C more recently.\nL38: ## About attribution with your unique Shop ID\nL39: \nL40: Your TikTok Shop has a unique ID that helps attribute orders and ad engagement for your shop. When someone places an order, we'll attribute the order to any ad clicks or views for the same Shop ID in the last 7 days.\nL41: We don't use a product ID for TikTok Shop Ads attribution. If someone sees an ad for one of your products, then buys a different product from your shop, the order will still be attributed to the ad. Both the order and the ad are connected to your unique Shop ID.\nL42: For example, someone clicks an ad from a different shop, and then orders a pair of sweatpants from your shop later that day. The order will not be attributed to the ad they clicked, because the ad is connected to a different Shop ID than the product they ordered.\nL43: \nL44: Note:\nL45: \nL46:   * We do not use a product ID for attribution\nL47: \nL48:   * We do not consider format for attribution\nL49: \nL50:   * We do not consider affiliate creator vs. non-affiliate creator\nL51: \nL52:   * We do not consider placement\nL53:   * A single order can not be attributed to multiple ads\nL54: \nL55: 【4†Image†lf16-tiktok-common.tiktokcdn-us.com】\nL56: \nL57: Log in for a personalised experience\nL58: \nL59: 【5†Sign up†ads.tiktok.com】\nL60: \nL61: Resources\nL62: \nL63: * 【6†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL64: * 【7†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL65: * 【8†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL66: * 【9†TikTok for Business†ads.tiktok.com】\nL67: * 【10†Creative Center†ads.tiktok.com】\nL68: \nL69: * 【11†Terms and Policies】\nL70: * 【12†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL71: \nL72: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n"
